[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "2607211000"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami maturity /loop session summary — ISCO occupation-side build-time demo rollout (iterations 1–17), cockpit-isic-5820 non-integration finding, session closing"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-20"
  :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki" "Claude Code (/loop)"]
  :adr/body
  "# Summary\n\nThis ADR closes out a single long-running Claude Code session that ran ADR-2607189200's cloud-itonami maturity-improvement charter across 17 iterations (2026-07-18 → 2026-07-20), first as dynamic self-paced `/loop`, then as a local `*/15 * * * *` session-only cron (job `41b23d8c`, now cancelled — session closing). Full blow-by-blow detail lives in `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-maturity-loop.md`; this ADR is the durable, queryable summary of what was decided and what state was left behind.\n\n# Portfolio-level finding (iter1–3, superseded nothing, still holds)\n\nPortfolio BMC/YC score improvement for cloud-itonami (revenue/validation/distribution axes, `maturity-scores.edn`) is hard-gated on `:hyp/itonami-smb-pay` (externalPaid>=1) — a real ¥80k/month Stripe subscription that only the human owner can create (safety-floor ②, real money movement). Live `/api/fleet/metrics` confirmed the technical conversion path (Stripe Payment Link, nudge automation, checkout preflight) is fully green; the only remaining bottleneck is the owner actually clicking Subscribe. This is NOT agent-actionable and the loop deliberately did not attempt it. Portfolio score remains at BMC 78 / YC 56.7 (2026-07-15 baseline) — unchanged this session, by design, not by oversight.\n\n# Pivot: within-product vertical maturity (owner-approved, iter3)\n\nGiven the above, the owner explicitly chose (iter3 decision point) to have the loop continue raising `cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`'s per-vertical Impl-product/Business axes via real, verifiable code — the only code-actionable lever available.\n\n# ISIC-side work (iter4–8)\n\n- Landed `POST /approve` (escalation-resume HTTP endpoint) on `cloud-itonami-isic-5820` (CRM flagship), closing a documented HTTP-layer gap; full test coverage, west.yml pin advanced.\n- **Key finding (iter8, corrects an earlier wrong assumption from iter6):** `cloud-itonami-isic-5820`'s \"live face\" referenced in `cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn` is NOT served by the cockpit worker (`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami`, the live multi-tenant itonami.cloud SaaS). The cockpit has **zero dependency** on isic-5820 (confirmed via `deps.edn` grep and `public/_redirects`/`open-business.json` registry inspection — isic-5820 is not in either). The \"live face\" is actually isic-5820's own **independent GitHub Pages static demo**, which structurally cannot run the repo's Clojure `crm/http.clj` server regardless of any pin/redeploy. Making the CRM's HTTP capabilities genuinely reachable from itonami.cloud would require new integration work (a cockpit proxy route, or a real Cloudflare Workers deploy path for isic-5820 itself) that does not exist today — **this is an open owner-level design/scoping decision, not resolved by this session** (see \"Left open for the owner\" below). The cockpit's own deploy pipeline was also found to be effectively dead (GitHub Actions disabled at the repo level; real deploys depend on a local `lefthook` post-merge hook on whichever machine happens to have this repo checked out with `wrangler login` done).\n\n# ISCO-side work (iter9–17) — the session's main sustained output\n\nAdapted the already-proven ISIC-side build-time-generated-demo pattern (`cloud-itonami-flagship-generator-template.edn`, proven on isic-851/isic-6820, since scaled by a separate automated \"Wave5\" process to 56+ ISIC repos) to the ISCO (occupation-code) side of the fleet, which has its own distinct but internally consistent actor shape: `src/<domain>/{governor,actor,advisor,store}.cljc` (4 files, vs ISIC's 7-file `facts/phase/sim/governor/operation/advisor/store` shape).\n\n**Scaling arc**: 1 repo (iter9, isco-1211) → 1 repo (iter10, isco-1111) → batch of 3 (iter11) → 6 (iter12) → 8 (iter14) → 10 (iter15) → 10-attempted/5-delivered due to an agent internal Group A/B split coordination failure (iter16) → 10-attempted/4-delivered due to the agent hitting a session weekly usage limit mid-run (iter17, partial). **39 ISCO repos landed and independently re-verified this session** (curl + sha256 match against every agent's claimed hash, not just trusted from reports) out of an original 126-repo no-demo backlog — 87 remain.\n\n**Discipline maintained throughout** (mirrors the ISIC-side precedent):\n- Real seed/scenario data sourced from each repo's own existing test fixtures, never invented; any deliberately-added extra entity disclosed explicitly in the code's own docstring.\n- Structurally-unreachable governor rules (via the real mock-advisor) disclosed honestly rather than faked or silently dropped.\n- 4-point verification bar on every repo: idempotent local rerun, from-scratch clean-checkout byte-match, live `workflow_dispatch` run success with its own regenerate step confirming no-diff, live GitHub Pages actually serving byte-identical content — the orchestrating session independently re-`curl`'d and hash-checked every single one of the 39, not just the sub-agents' say-so.\n- Stub / shape-mismatch / broken repos correctly screened OUT rather than force-fit: `isco-0210`, `isco-0310`, `isco-1322`, `isco-2146`, `isco-3121` (explicit `{:stub true}` or \"Simplified stub\" markers, zero real `langgraph.graph` usage), `isco-3134` (older 5-file layout, out of this template's scope).\n- **3 real pre-existing bugs found during screening and fixed at their root cause** (not worked around, not silently excluded): `isco-2111` (physics — mock-advisor dropped `:finalized?`/`:novel?` request keys entirely, compounded by a test itself never actually passing the flag it claimed to test), `isco-8343` and `isco-9329` (commit-node accepted a `store` param but never called `store/add-record!`, so the audit ledger was silently never populated despite docstrings claiming an append-only trail). All three verified green (before/after test counts) both by the fixing agent and, for the isco-2111 case, independently by the orchestrating session.\n\n# Operational incidents this session (all handled, all documented for future sessions)\n\n1. **Session log content loss**: the running session-log file (`cloud-itonami-maturity-loop.md`) briefly lost its iteration 5–7 narrative to concurrent-session churn in the shared superproject checkout (the underlying *code* work was never lost — verified independently against each child repo's own git history — only this session's prose记録 of it). Backfilled from verified git evidence in iter8.\n2. **Shared-checkout concurrency**: this exact superproject root checkout is under near-continuous fast-forward-merge churn from many other parallel sessions/automated routines (observed 20+ merges/hour at peak) — confirmed via reflog, not an anomaly. Per CLAUDE.md's \"統合・閲覧専用\" rule, every actual code/doc change this session was made in an isolated sibling `git worktree` (outside the superproject root) and landed via server-side `gh api .../merges`, never by editing the shared root directly.\n3. **`manifest/west.yml` pin-advance races**: multiple 409 conflicts and one fleet-wide pin-regression discovery (unrelated repos: `cofog-05.1/06.3/07.4`, `ai-gftd-*`, etc., caused by *other* sessions' wholesale regenerations against stale local checkouts — a known anti-pattern per CLAUDE.md, self-healing via repeated re-advance commits from whichever session next noticed). This session's own pin advances always used the single-entry GitHub-API-PUT pattern with fresh blob-sha re-fetch on 409, never a wholesale regen.\n4. **Uncommitted WIP found in the shared root checkout**: another session's uncommitted `west.yml` edits (`iso3166-usa-*` pins) were found blocking a `git merge --ff-only`; preserved via `git stash push` (not dropped) per CLAUDE.md's explicit guidance — several other `other-session-WIP-*` stashes were already present from other concurrent sessions, suggesting a fleet-wide stash pile that may warrant a future `git-cleanup-conflict` triage pass (out of scope for this session).\n5. **Agent self-splitting coordination failure (iter16)**: a batch agent internally split itself into \"Group A\"/\"Group B\" sub-agents; only Group B's final report ever reached the orchestrating session, Group A's outcome is genuinely unknown (reported as such, not guessed at). Subsequent iterations (17) were explicitly instructed not to repeat this.\n6. **Session weekly usage limit hit (iter17)**: a batch agent was terminated mid-run by a `\"You've hit your weekly limit · resets 12pm (Asia/Tokyo)\"` API error. Rather than trust its terse last-progress note, the orchestrating session independently verified against GitHub which of its target repos had actually landed (4 of 5 had; the 5th had no branch/no Pages, confirming nothing was lost, just not started) before advancing pins for the confirmed ones. No further background agents were spawned for the remainder of that session to avoid immediately re-hitting the same wall.\n7. Harness-managed nested `isolation:\"worktree\"` agent worktrees under `.claude/worktrees/agent-*` repeatedly failed plain `git worktree remove` with a non-standard `.git`-is-not-a-gitfile error; per CLAUDE.md's caution against forcing destructive operations on ambiguous shared state, these were left for the harness/owner rather than force-deleted.\n\n# Left open for the owner (not resolved by this session, by design)\n\n1. **First paid checkout** — portfolio revenue/validation/distribution axes stay flat until the owner completes one real Stripe subscription via `/isco-1212` (or `/isic-6399`, `/isic-6310`). Preflight is green.\n2. **cockpit ↔ isic-5820 integration design** — decide whether isic-5820 (and by extension every other ISIC/ISCO repo whose \"live face\" is really just its own GitHub Pages demo) should (a) stay self-host-only with the static demo accepted as the ceiling of \"live\", or (b) get real integration work (cockpit proxy route, or its own Cloudflare Workers deploy path). This is a scope/budget decision, not a bounded one-iteration bump.\n3. **ISCO no-demo backlog**: 87 of the original 126 repos remain untouched (no stub/bug/shape issues found in any of them yet — simply not yet screened). The proven methodology (this ADR + `cloud-itonami-maturity-loop.md` iterations 9–17) can be resumed by any future session using the same batch-agent pattern once the weekly usage limit resets.\n4. **Fleet-wide stash pile** — several `other-session-WIP-*` stashes have accumulated in the shared superproject root checkout from this and other concurrent sessions (see incident 4 above). Not triaged this session; candidate for a future `git-cleanup-conflict` pass.\n\n# Session closing\n\nThe local session-only cron job (`41b23d8c`, `*/15 * * * *`) is being cancelled as part of closing this session — it would die with the session regardless, but is stopped explicitly here for a clean record. Superproject root checkout confirmed synced to `origin/main` at session end. No uncommitted changes, no open feature branches under this session's control left on GitHub (all merged-and-deleted per iteration). This ADR plus `cloud-itonami-maturity-loop.md`'s iterations 1–17 are the complete, honest record of this session's work — no fabricated numbers, no silently-skipped failures, no claimed-but-unverified live states."}]
